  "summary": "Sundanese traditional house refers to the traditional vernacular houses of the Sundanese people, who predominantly inhabited the western part of Java island, Indonesia.",
  "description": "Sundanese traditional house refers to the traditional vernacular houses of the Sundanese people, who predominantly inhabited the western part of Java island, Indonesia. The architecture of a Sundanese house is characterized by its functionality, simplicity, modesty, uniformity with a little detail, its use of natural thatched materials, and the quite faithful adherence to harmony with nature and the environment.",
